---
title: Tissue Curation
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

Tissue curation checks specimen part tubes—and optionally symbiont tubes—into
storage boxes. For each tube you scan or place, NAHPU writes a museum code to
`Museum permanent` or `Museum loan` and assigns the next free cell as its
`Storage location` (such as `Box 1: D1`), keeping database records aligned with
physical freezer boxes without manual typing.

